---
title: Widget primitives
---

<script>
  import Demo from "$lib/docs/Demo.svelte";
</script>

Every `WidgetView.body` entry is one of these. The previews below are rendered
by the same logic the app uses.

## text

A line of copy. `tone`: `default` · `muted` · `primary`.

<Demo node={{ kind: "text", text: "3 workouts this week — one short of your target.", tone: "muted" }} />

## stat-grid

Up to three headline numbers.

<Demo node={{ kind: "stat-grid", stats: [
  { label: "This week", value: "12,480 kg" },
  { label: "Sets", value: "48" },
  { label: "PRs", value: "2" },
]}} />

## list

Rows with an optional sublabel, trailing text, and a tap action.

<Demo node={{ kind: "list", items: [
  { label: "Mon 31 Aug", sublabel: "Top: Bench 3×80", trailing: "42m", action: { navigate: "/sessions/x" } },
  { label: "Fri 28 Aug", sublabel: "Top: Squat 5×100", trailing: "51m", action: { navigate: "/sessions/y" } },
], emptyText: "No sessions yet." }} />

## progress-rings

One ring per target.

<Demo node={{ kind: "progress-rings", rings: [
  { label: "Calories", value: 1450, max: 2200, unit: "kcal" },
  { label: "Protein", value: 90, max: 160, unit: "g" },
]}} />

## bar

Horizontal bars. `sublabel` overrides the value text; `tone`: `primary` ·
`protein` · `carbs` · `fat`.

<Demo node={{ kind: "bar", bars: [
  { label: "Calories", value: 1450, max: 2200, sublabel: "1450 / 2200 kcal", tone: "primary" },
  { label: "Protein", value: 90, max: 160, sublabel: "90 / 160 g", tone: "protein" },
  { label: "Carbs", value: 140, max: 240, sublabel: "140 / 240 g", tone: "carbs" },
  { label: "Fat", value: 55, max: 70, sublabel: "55 / 70 g", tone: "fat" },
]}} />

## line

A trend line with an optional horizontal `reference` (e.g. a goal weight).

<Demo node={{ kind: "line", reference: 78, points: [
  { x: 0, y: 82 }, { x: 1, y: 81.4 }, { x: 2, y: 81 }, { x: 3, y: 80.6 },
  { x: 4, y: 80.1 }, { x: 5, y: 79.6 }, { x: 6, y: 79.2 },
]}} />

## muscle-map

A front/back body map. `values` is effort per muscle group; `scale` is the three
band thresholds (default `[1, 5, 12]`).

<Demo node={{ kind: "muscle-map", scale: [1, 5, 12], values: {
  chest: 14, triceps: 7, shoulders: 4, back: 2, biceps: 1,
}}} />

## calendar-heatmap

A month grid; `days` are the days with activity.

<Demo node={{ kind: "calendar-heatmap", month: "2026-09", days: [
  { day: 2 }, { day: 4 }, { day: 7 }, { day: 9 }, { day: 12 }, { day: 15 }, { day: 18 }, { day: 21 },
]}} />

## button-row

Full-width stacked buttons. `primary` fills one.

<Demo node={{ kind: "button-row", buttons: [
  { label: "Start today's plan", action: { startPlannedWorkout: true }, primary: true },
  { label: "Start unplanned", action: { startEmptyWorkout: true } },
]}} />

---

Need a primitive that isn't here? The vocabulary is deliberately small — open an
issue with the use case.
